  "id": "head-rolling",
  "term": "head rolling",
  "definition": "Head rolling is a head-tilting movement discussed in vestibulo-ocular research, where gravity can activate neck muscles and stretch jaw muscles through the mandible and related tissue connections. In this context, it may contribute sensory input that interacts with vestibular signals involved in vertical-torsional eye movement control.",
